[2] This is an application under Article 226 of the Constitution of India fo seeking the following relief(s):
 (i) Issue Rule NISI calling upon the respondents and each of them, to  as to why a Writ of Certiorari and/or in the nature thereof shall not be issued, for calling upon the records pertaining to the instant matter;
(ii) Issue Rule NISI calling upon the respondents to show cause as to why a writ in the nature of Mandamus shall not be issued mandating/directing the Respondents to conduct an enquiry with regard to the applications dated 11.11.2024 (Annexure 7 supra) and .11.2024 (Annexure 8 supra) of the petitioner for releasing the compensation amount in favour of the petitioner under the National Highways Act, 1956 for acquisition of the land measuring 0.0404694 hectors under Hal Dag No.
4708 within Khatian No. 1438/1 and to rectify the error in the record of right, within a time frame;
Smt. Anju Rani Sukla Das vs The Project Director on 9 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/55630168/
1 (iii) Issue Rule NISI calling upon the respondents to show cause as to why a writ in the nature of Prohibition shall not be issued prohibiting/restraining the Respondents from releasing the award of the land to any other person except the petitioner who is the physical and forceful possessor of the land;
AND (iv) After hearing the parties be pleased to make the Rule absolute, issuing direction to the respondent;
AND (v) Pass any order or orders as Lordship may fit and proper in favour of the petitioner.
